    <GaugingStation location="Upton" name="Haddeo" number="45816">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Flat V weir opened in 1993.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">No bypassing or drowning out. Considered a good station. Station just upstream of Wimbleball Reservoir. Bankfull at 1.6m. One rating applied across period of record confirmed to 0.5m by spot flow gaugings.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Station opened in 01/1993 with a Flat V weir, crest length approximately 5m wide. Relatively straight approach with a stable bed. Velocity area station for higher flows.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2022 (WINFAP Files v11).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Wimbleball Reservoir is just a few meters downstream.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Relatively small catchment area consisting mostly of Upper Devonian sandstones, siltstones and slates. Land use is mainly rural and agricultural. No major urbanisation in the catchment. Wimbleball Reservoir impounded 1978.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff"/>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Good fit to rating." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Although only confirmed to 0.5m, structure is thought to perform well at flows beyond QMED and valid to bankfull." suitable="Yes" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
